# Try the API from Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code (REST Client). Start it with `docker compose up --build`.
@bank = http://localhost:8080

### Open an account
# @name open
POST {{bank}}/api/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "owner": "Ana Souza", "currency": "BRL" }

###
@id = {{open.response.body.$.accountId}}

### Deposit
POST {{bank}}/api/accounts/{{id}}/deposits
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 1500.00, "description": "Salary" }

### Withdraw (try more than the balance to see 422)
POST {{bank}}/api/accounts/{{id}}/withdrawals
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 200.00, "description": "ATM" }

### Read model: summary and statement
GET {{bank}}/api/accounts/{{id}}

###
GET {{bank}}/api/accounts/{{id}}/statement

### The raw event stream
GET {{bank}}/api/accounts/{{id}}/events

### All accounts (the sample data has six weeks of history)
GET {{bank}}/api/accounts

### Balance at a past moment: replays the stream up to "at".
# The account opened above did not exist yet on that date (404). Paste a sample account id to see an older balance.
GET {{bank}}/api/accounts/{{id}}/balance?at=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z
